{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1542147-weather-themed-things","id":1542147,"title":"Weather themed things","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-14T16:47:09-07:00","id":1542147,"title":"Weather themed things","content":"I\u2019m looking for some more weather inspired regalia/kith/stuff in general for a storm elemental I\u2019m creating set in an 1800\u2019s pirate game. I am lacking on resources and don\u2019t really know where to look to find stuff like that. So any help is appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28463-bwhite24","name":"Bwhite24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T17:57:59-07:00","id":1542149,"title":"","content":"The codex of darkness wiki can help with not having too many book sources.<br /> <br /> For Kiths, there are the Climacteric that can predict the weather, Absinthial that can make Rum and other alcoholic beverages, Asclepian that can help with the eyepatchs and wooden legs aesthetics, Chevalier that could bond with ships and call them to their side as if they were living beings, Farwalkers that could make a home in every port, Nymphs, Swimmerskin and Uttervoice that could take the role of the classical mermaids. Of course, you could also create your own Kith.<br /> <br /> Regalia I would advise the Steed, since it deals a lot with transportation, if you want to cause Enviromental Tilts(like storms), there is a contract on the Sword regalia for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 09-14-2024, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T18:05:28-07:00","id":1542152,"title":"","content":"In many Mediterranean and African traditions supernatural beings travel in whirlwind. Dust devils, even in many places in Europe, are still said to be some type of local supernatural being passing by. Such statements are rarely believed anymore, but it's a sign of an old belief. <br /> <br /> By the by, one of the most popular superheroines, Storm, gets her look from what anthropologists call a witch and we would call a fairy. Notice that Storm's hair is the color of clouds in a summer sky. Storm's eyes are sky colored. In several folk traditions in East Africa this marks her as a supernatural being that controls the weather. Thus a person from a dark skinned ethnic group with platinum blond hair and sky blue eyes would be marked as a weather fay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T18:13:59-07:00","id":1542153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bwhite24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1542147-weather-themed-things#post1542147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m looking for some more weather inspired regalia/kith/stuff in general for a storm elemental I\u2019m creating set in an 1800\u2019s pirate game. I am lacking on resources and don\u2019t really know where to look to find stuff like that. So any help is appreciated!</div> </div> </div> </div>Pirates were less common in most of the planet in the 1800s. The Barbary Pirates were around for awhile, but are restricted to coastal attacks from southern Morocco after 1830. China had Pirates. They mainly let themselves be bought out. Pirates in the Caribbean were mainly smugglers. Most robberies they carried out were on land. The British navy was to dangerous. <br /> <br /> I'd more your Pirate Campaign back to sometime in the 1660 to 1740 period. Remember, in the last twenty years of that period, pirates were nearly wiped out. The Barbary Pirates were the exception in the Atlantic. They took ships in sight of Dover in this period and sold the passengers as slaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T06:44:43-07:00","id":1542365,"title":"","content":"If you really want to dig deep into Caribbean piracy, I recommend the <i>7th Sea</i> supplement <a href=\"https://www.chaosium.com/7th-sea-pirate-nations-hardcover/?srsltid=AfmBOor1xLDwGkNK8gMSfig9zViElsNYe6ERFIVXZrYUcVAaNf7ZlWMv\" target=\"_blank\">Pirate Nations</a>. It's not historically accurate by any stretch, but probably better suited to a semi-historical chronicle than most fantasy TTRPG sourcebooks. It's useful for Changeling specifically because it provides rules for drawing up <i>charters</i>: magically binding contracts to which each member of a pirate crew voluntarily binds themselves.<br /> <br /> For <i>vampiric</i> pirates there's the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/266801-bloodline-tregarthen\">Tregarthen bloodline</a> that TheKingsRaven created. He also wrote up a partial set of CtL 1e &quot;Contacts of Ship and Sail,&quot; which I can only find in <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a>. In fact, I probably should have led by mentioning that collection of aquatic fan-made material, since I've kind of adopted it as my own passion project.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}